  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "direct judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D016 unclear",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D025 unclear",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D030 unclear",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D032 unclear",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D068 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "Classify as not-faithful-weaker. Lean does not recover the source's directional numerical-solve semantics. The reverse implication nevertheless holds because the exact quantified Lean conclusion follows from its supplied definitions and structural input assumptions alone. The round-trip judge's observation that the source does not state this generic theorem establishes lack of faithful representation, but does not establish failure of logical implication.",
      "primary_evidence": "D013 and D018 construct the schedule; D023 supplies nonemptiness and exhaustive coverage; D020–D021 encode finite sequential execution; D024 applies already supplied total functions. Section 1.3, printed page 6, instead describes solving one-dimensional coordinate problems in turn."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Confirm the principal solver-semantic failure independently. A map A(r,s)(c) = s(c0), for a fixed cell c0, satisfies the entire D022 constant-preservation requirement. It ignores the fraction and can mix data across coordinate lines. Its scheduled execution satisfies the target without establishing any directional numerical solve. The geometric question remains separately limited by the source's undefined terminology.",
      "primary_evidence": "D022 has only a total update function and its constant-preservation law. D019 adds direction indexing and bounded positive fractions, with no grid compatibility predicate. Section 1.3 requires one-dimensional problems along coordinate directions."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Confirm rejection but correct the reverse implication and moderate the restriction claim. Exactly-once traversal and fractions in (0,1] are formal scheduling conventions, not consequences explicitly asserted by the passage. They are assumptions or construction choices within the theorem, however, rather than assertions that every source method satisfies these restrictions. They therefore do not refute the reverse implication for this independently derivable proposition.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target universally quantifies over supplied grid and method structures before asserting existence of schedule, finalState, and trace. D019 contains the fraction assumptions, and D023 contains the direction enumeration assumptions. The source specifies neither numerical fractions nor a detailed repetition pattern."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
      "resolution": "The declaration meaning is determined: the grid packages a measurable partition, exhaustive ordered directions, coordinate geometry, and positive-width coordinate-box cells. Only its direction family appears in the target conclusion. Whether the full package is equivalent to every source logically rectangular grid remains unestablished; this does not obstruct interpretation of the target or its generic execution consequence.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 is specified by constructor D016, with partition constructor D034 and direction constructor D023. D002 projects the direction family. The elaborated conclusion accesses grid.coordinateDirections and no other grid field."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D016 unclear",
      "resolution": "The constructor imposes genuine box and partition conditions, so the grid is not merely a geometry label. Those conditions are expressed in supplied coordinates and do not add regularity or compatibility of the updates with the grid. Full correspondence with the source's logical-grid condition remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "D016 requires strictly ordered real faces and equality of each partition region with D030. D034 requires measurability, disjointness, and exact coverage of a chosen domain. No constructor argument links grid geometry to D022 updates."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D025 unclear",
      "resolution": "Its two cases are exactly a type equality with real coordinate tuples and a set-theoretic equivalence with those tuples. The equality case yields an equivalence by transport; the other case returns the supplied equivalence. These are fully interpretable alternatives, but their names do not certify the source's geometric meaning.",
      "primary_evidence": "D032–D033 give the two constructors. D031 and D036–D038 perform case elimination; D079 supplies Equiv.cast. Section 1.3 names rectangular and logically rectangular grids without defining the latter on the attached pages."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D030 unclear",
      "resolution": "The definition is precisely the inverse image of a half-open coordinate box. Exhaustiveness of the direction list makes every coordinate inequality applicable. Half-open boundaries coherently support disjoint cells. Positive widths and coordinate surjectivity make every full-grid cell nonempty. None of these facts establishes additional physical regularity of logical coordinates.",
      "primary_evidence": "D030 requires lowerFace(d) ≤ coordinates(point)(d) < upperFace(d) for every listed direction. D023 makes the list exhaustive; D016 supplies positive widths; D031 supplies a bijection. D034 supplies set disjointness."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D032 unclear",
      "resolution": "It accepts any bijection, without continuity, differentiability, or measurable-map requirements. Requiring the selected cell inverse images to be measurable does not supply those omitted map properties. The attached source does not determine which additional geometric conditions, if any, are needed for an equivalent definition of logical rectangularity. Preserve this source-correspondence uncertainty.",
      "primary_evidence": "D032 takes only Equiv Point (Direction → Real). D016 and D034 add box-region equality and cell measurability, but no topological structure or coordinate-map regularity. Printed page 6 provides no definition resolving this issue."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D068 unclear",
      "resolution": "Reinterpret the reused dependency in this task: Equiv supplies forward and inverse coordinate functions with inverse laws. The reused Matrix.of phrase is irrelevant. D067, D069, and D070 evaluate the forward coordinate map; they add no geometric regularity. Declaration meaning is resolved, while adequacy as a model of source logical rectangularity remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "D031–D032 use Equiv Point (Direction → Real). D069 explicitly selects Equiv.toFun and Equiv.invFun; D070 retains the forward coercion; D067 projects that function. The inline reuse ledger's earlier Matrix.of context supplies no task-specific geometric evidence."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve the formal boundary behavior: empty direction types and empty cell index types cannot supply the required grid; positive-width boxes are nonempty; fraction one is allowed and nonpositive fractions are excluded. Singleton direction families remain allowed. Half-open cell boundaries are coherent. The only remaining issue here is equivalence of the logical-coordinate representation to the undefined source geometry. Absence of practical exceptions from a trace-existence theorem is omission, not an assertion of universal numerical sufficiency.",
      "primary_evidence": "D017, D019, D023, D030–D034 specify these cases. Section 1.3, printed pages 6–7, qualifies practical effectiveness and acknowledges cases requiring a more fully multidimensional method. The target contains no effectiveness or sufficiency predicate."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The changes of scope are identifiable: arbitrary Value types and arbitrary constant-preserving maps broaden the objects beyond numerical solvers; nonempty finite directions include the one-dimensional case; global coordinate bijections and a once-per-direction positive-fraction sweep select a particular representation. These changes supply no genuine stronger numerical result. Exact coverage of source logically rectangular grids remains uncertain, but cannot repair the independent failure already present on ordinary rectangular grids.",
      "primary_evidence": "D011, D019, D022, D023, and D032 expose the relevant domains and restrictions. Section 1.3 concerns extending one-dimensional high-resolution numerical methods to multiple dimensions in the stated grid setting."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, relation strength, execution semantics, and reused elementary dependencies",
      "resolution": "The inputs are satisfiable with Direction = Fin 2, Point = Direction → Real, a finite rectangular grid of half-open unit cells, real values, identity updates, and fractions one. Nonconstant states and constant-preserving broadcast updates are also admitted. Thus rejection rests on loss of numerical meaning, not impossible premises. The execution relation correctly feeds each output into the next step, and its equalities concern schedule data and trace counts rather than exact PDE evolution. D050 correctly excludes empty lists and distinguishes indices; D055 supplies the literal natural one in the trace count. No analytic existence or uniqueness claim should be attributed to this operational existence theorem.",
      "primary_evidence": "D020–D021 and D024 specify sequential execution. D050 unfolds to negated equality; D055 interprets natural literals directly. D022 permits identity and broadcast maps. The target has no PDE solution operator, approximation estimate, or well-posedness predicate."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "Even on an ordinary two-dimensional rectangular grid with nonconstant real cell data, the permitted updates can broadcast a selected cell's value to every cell for every fraction and direction. D022 accepts these maps because they preserve constants. D019 and the target add no relation to a governing hyperbolic problem, coordinate-line solves, or a high-resolution finite volume method. Correctly scheduling and executing such maps therefore does not establish the source's defining numerical operation. This failure persists independently of the unresolved logical-grid interpretation and of whether the paragraph's practical assessments are included as formal conclusions."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "With the supplied Lean definitions admitted, fix any grid, method, and initialState satisfying the quantified input types. Map method.fractionalStep over the grid's direction list. Its nonemptiness and exhaustive directional coverage follow from D023 and the copied fields in D018. Define successive states by applying each stored total update at its stored fraction. The constructors D020–D021 produce an execution ending at the last state, with the initial state and one state after every step, hence exactly schedule.length + 1 entries. This argument derives the complete proposition from its structural assumptions without any substantive source premise. Consequently the source entails this weaker proposition in that background. It does not follow that the source identifies arbitrary maps as numerical solvers or endorses every formal modeling convention."
    }
  },
  "classification": "not-faithful-weaker",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The attached primary-source pages do not define logical rectangularity sufficiently to establish equivalence with arbitrary global coordinate bijections and measurable inverse images of half-open boxes. The Lean declaration meanings are clear; their complete geometric correspondence remains unresolved."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "missing-directional-solver-semantics",
      "evidence": "Section 1.3, printed page 6, defines successive one-dimensional coordinate solves. D022 requires only a total real-parameterized state map preserving constants; D019 only assigns such maps to direction labels.",
      "impact": "The target admits updates unrelated to directional numerical problems, so its conclusion cannot recover the source's defining operation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "generic-execution-substituted-for-numerical-construction",
      "evidence": "D013, D018, D020–D021, and D024 yield the schedule and execution history for any supplied total maps. Constant preservation and the grid's geometric fields are unnecessary for that existence-and-length conclusion.",
      "impact": "The theorem is a nonvacuous generic execution fact whose truth bypasses the intended numerical content. This supports not-faithful-weaker rather than faithful-stronger."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "missing-finite-volume-role-linkage",
      "evidence": "Section 1.2, printed page 5, describes numerical cell averages and flux-based updates. D011 is only Cell → Value, and neither D022 nor the target links updates to the partition or to a finite volume problem.",
      "impact": "A function type can represent numerical data, but the supplied contract does not establish the relevant numerical roles. Imported averaging definitions outside the target's semantic dependencies do not supply that missing connection."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "unresolved-geometric-correspondence",
      "evidence": "D032 accepts a bare equivalence; D030 pulls back coordinate boxes; D034 requires cell measurability. Section 1.3 does not define logical rectangularity on the attached pages.",
      "impact": "Complete geometric equivalence cannot be certified. Rejection and the implication classification do not depend on resolving this uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "classification-and-scope-correction",
      "evidence": "The round-trip judgment treats absence of the generic theorem from the prose and added input restrictions as grounds for source_implies_translation = no. The declaration itself makes those restrictions antecedent input data and has a conclusion derivable by finite recursion.",
      "impact": "Unsupported representation choices prevent faithful equivalence, but do not refute the reverse logical implication here. Schedule conventions are not stronger numerical conclusions, and trace existence is not universal practical sufficiency."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached source images and the supplied declaration evidence confirms genuine sequential execution and exhaustive direction coverage, but no semantic guarantee that the executed maps solve one-dimensional coordinate problems. The decisive counterexample satisfies the formal assumptions on an ordinary rectangular grid, so uncertainty about logical rectangularity does not undermine rejection. The complete Lean proposition follows from finite-list construction under its own input assumptions; this resolves the judges' classification disagreement in favor of not-faithful-weaker. Remaining geometric uncertainty is retained explicitly. No tools were used, no target proof was needed, and the supplied provenance hashes were not independently recomputed."
}
